{
  "_comment": "Hand-authored fixture for a tuple return. Mirrors the layout juliac emits for `JLWResult{CTuple2{CVector{:owned,Float64},Int64}}`, with one @ccallable function returning it, plus the macro-emitted jlw_free/jlw_free_strings release entrypoints so the owning element is `:auto` (copy, then free in a `finally`), not `:mechanical`. It exists to exercise a tuple return whose first element owns its storage and whose second does not, so the emitter has to convert the two elements by different kinds and release only the first. Offsets probed from the real JLWInterop layout: sizeof(CTuple2{CVector{:owned,Float64},Int64})=24, fieldoffset 0/16; sizeof(JLWStatus)=260; sizeof(JLWResult{CTuple2{...}})=288, fieldoffset 0/264.",
